WEBVTT

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:01.287
And I often look at things
as though they're food.

00:12:01.311 --> 00:12:03.554
Like, I say, "Would you serve
a rotten chicken?

00:12:03.578 --> 00:12:06.299
Then how could you serve
a beat-up old dress or something?

00:12:06.323 --> 00:12:08.288
How could you show a beat-up old dress?"

00:12:08.312 --> 00:12:11.039
I always relate things to kitchen-ry.

00:12:11.063 --> 00:12:12.126
(Laughter)

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:15.108
And so I think
that's what it all boils down to.

00:12:15.132 --> 00:12:16.690
Everything boils down to that.

00:12:16.714 --> 00:12:17.871
So check this out.

00:12:17.895 --> 00:12:19.280
This is what I've been doing,

00:12:19.304 --> 00:12:21.785
because I think it's the most
fun thing in the world.

00:12:21.809 --> 00:12:24.721
It's, like, this website
with a lot of different things on it.

00:12:24.745 --> 00:12:26.285
It's a polymathematical website.

00:12:26.309 --> 00:12:29.436
We actually shoot segments,
like TV show segments.

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:32.344
And it's kind of my favorite
thing in the world.